# golden for tests/probes/bus-words.bund
# captured by `cargo xtask golden` from reference/Bund via target/oracle
# normalised: id and stamp (F14), dict member order (F15), ANSI stripped
# verified: two oracle runs produced identical output
## exit
0
## output
probe: send answers a bool, and the value comes back
probe: in exists before the program does, so it is empty and not absent
probe: bus.data creates the channel it reports on
probe: bus.data.current names the channel after the current stack
probe: send.quick answers nothing
probe: send. takes the object from the workbench, the name from the stack
probe: recv. takes the name from the workbench and pushes to the stack
probe: send.quick. takes the object from the workbench and answers nothing
probe: a channel keeps order
